  "scope": "Direct normal-noise JSON decoding using the actual pinned vanilla CODEC. Every bundled noise registry resource, explicit/default parameters, empty and full amplitude modifiers, normalization modes, inclusive field bounds with signed-zero comparator ordering, malformed types, null fields, duplicate and ignored keys, decimal/exponent integer truncation and wrapping, signed zero, seeded modern/legacy and Nether construction, octave metadata, range and normalization bits, scalar noise values and parent random state. JSON resource contents stay private. Strict JSON parsing; no claim for Gson's permissive non-JSON syntax. Bundled density registries are also decoded with actual vanilla registry-aware CODECs: named forward references, all bundled function kinds, declared range/axes, raw compilation errors, seeded optimized roots, cache allocation, scalar values, strided bulk values, repeated cache hits and surface-volume errors are compared using RandomState's actual compile context. All seven bundled noise-setting resources contribute their actual eight-field NoiseRouter.CODEC objects to RandomState. Router fields are compiled in declaration order with a shared compiler/context; cache allocation, raw/optimized scalar and repeated strided volume values, successful single-layer surface volumes and invalid surface-volume shapes are compared. Actual RandomState climate sampler binding and quart-to-block coordinate wrapping are checked at ordinary and extreme positions. Float-to-long climate quantization and long-to-float conversion include subnormals, signed zeros, NaNs, infinities, cast saturation and seeded random bit patterns. Actual vanilla Climate.Parameter and ParameterPoint JSON codecs compare scalar, two-element list and min/max object intervals, float endpoint bounds/ordering, required coordinate/offset fields, negative zero, precision-sensitive float parsing, malformed types and duplicate keys. Climate parameter distances, wrapping squared fitness, stable search-tree leaf order and nearest lookup are compared across every supported branching value 2..32, sizes around branch powers, the 65536-entry API bound, duplicates, warm ties, fresh lookups, brute-force lookup and extreme signed-long endpoints/targets. The Rust tree is immutable with per-worker search state instead of hidden thread locals; invalid or degenerate searches return typed errors. Inline arbitrary distance metrics and behavior outside the bounded API are not covered. Built-in Overworld and Nether quantized biome parameter tables are exported independently by each authenticated JAR and required to agree before Rust consumes them. The Rust multi-noise resolver and actual vanilla MultiNoiseBiomeSource compare biome identities through scalar climate queries and prepared bulk quart volumes, including forward/reverse/repeated query order, wrapped extreme origins and shared previous-result state. Biome holder keys in the reference are registration placeholders; no biome property or gameplay behavior is evaluated. The Rust loader reads a Horizon quantized table format, not the vanilla biome codec, and the preset builders themselves have not been ported. Source and private fixture mutations during validation invalidate the report. The two-field 26.3 NoiseSettings codec, create helper and LevelHeightAccessor clamping are also compared across bundled noise members, dimension/alignment bounds, zero/negative runtime heights, disjoint ranges, wrapped integer arithmetic and decimal/exponent integer conversion. Global fluid cutoff selection and the actual disabled Aquifer implementation are compared with original default block-state identities, extreme sea levels/coordinates, signed-zero/subnormal/nonfinite density and counted picker calls; developer fluid-disable behavior is outside the regular-mode corpus. The actual noise-based Aquifer.Config codec and runtime are compared across bundled aquifer settings, modern/legacy world-seeded aquifer factories, synthetic density roots, nondefault water/lava states, cave/void air, nonfinite sampler overrides, strided volume extents, wrapped coordinates, repeated and reversed queries, counted picker calls, sampler call order/values, injected failures and retry state, scheduling flags, populated location/status caches and sorted surface-cache entries. Oversized or wrapped-invalid grid allocations and developer fluid-disable behavior are outside the bounded regular-mode API. Terrain filling is not yet validated. Router, vertical noise and optional aquifer members are decoded from each noise-setting resource; complete NoiseGeneratorSettings, material rules, nonempty world fields, biome registry/codecs and complete chunk biome assignment, generated chunks, gameplay and rendering remain pending. Inline noise holders and general codec behavior beyond the covered fixtures remain pending."
